        "file": "example.com.zone",
        "lang": "text",
        "kind": "vulnerable",
        "code": "$ORIGIN example.com.\n$TTL 3600\n\n@         IN  A      203.0.113.10\nwww       IN  CNAME  example.com.\n@         IN  MX     10 mail.example.com.\nmail      IN  A      203.0.113.25\n\n; Flaw 1: \"+all\" authorises EVERY server on the Internet to send mail as example.com\n@         IN  TXT    \"v=spf1 +all\"\n\n; Flaw 2: this alias points to a cloud resource that was deleted months ago.\n; Whoever re-creates \"shop-2019\" at the provider controls old-shop.example.com\nold-shop  IN  CNAME  shop-2019.cloud-provider.example.\n\n; Flaw 3: no DMARC record and no CAA record\n",
